    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0069" n="57" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg57"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.00/8–746: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Saigon</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Reed</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-09-09T14:00:00-04:00">September 9, 1946—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>241. Intelligence reports of uncertain reliability state USSR (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) anxious see Ho Chi Minh succeed unite three Kys
                    under Viet Nam for possible eventual weapon against National Govt China and (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>) has instructed French Communists manoeuvre
                    reliable French Officers to Indochina for training cadres future Viet Nam army.
                    Keep Dept informed indications subservience to Party line by Ho and other
                    leaders, relative strength Communist and non-Communist elements Viet Nam, and
                    contacts with Communists other countries. Inform O’Sullivan. Sent Saigon.
                    Repeated Paris<anchor n="59" xml:id="d71-f1"/> for info.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clayton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
